e = 42 + 5.5(Hours). What is the correct interpretation of the slope?","choices":[{"correct":true,"text":"On average, each additional hour studied is associated with 5.5 more points on the exam","feedback":"Correct! Each additional hour of study is associated, on average, with a 5.5-point increase in exam score."},{"correct":false,"text":"A student who studies 1 hour is predicted to score 42","feedback":"42 is the intercept—the predicted score for a student who studied 0 hours."},{"correct":false,"text":"Every student who studies one more hour will score exactly 5.5 points higher","feedback":"The slope describes an average change, not a guarantee for each individual student."}],"multi":false,"hint":"The slope is the average change in the response for a 1-unit increase in the explanatory variable.","explanation":""},"key":"UqlrTmNu9g"},{"type":"anywidget","esm":"/textbook/build/quiz-widget-612a97c1bdda77747487ee7393cbf45b.mjs","model":{"question":"Using the age-distance regression line Distance = 576 − 3(Age), what is the predicted legibility distance for a 40-year-old driver?","choices":[{"correct":true,"text":"456 feet","feedback":"Correct! 576 − 3(40) = 576 − 120 = 456 feet."},{"correct":false,"text":"476 feet","feedback":"Check the arithmetic: 3 × 40 = 120, and 576 − 120 = 456."},{"correct":false,"text":"536 feet","feedback":"Remember to multiply the age by the slope before subtracting."}],"multi":false,"hint":"Substitute Age = 40 into the equation.","explanation":""},"key":"F03FTebcd7"}],"key":"cnUtwlSRpo"}],"key":"NVPcHfywDD"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Least Squares: Finding the Best-Fitting Line","url":"/pages/m05-linear-relationships-6-of-8","group":"Section 4: Examining Relationships"},"next":{"title":"Predicting with Care: Interpolation vs. Extrapolation","url":"/pages/m05-linear-relationships-8-of-8","group":"Section 4: Examining Relationships"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}